like she was very sweet.

00:07:52.255 --> 00:07:55.260
Her name was not Olga, I did ask her that,

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.810
but I couldn't figure out her actual name.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.300
So, I asked if it was
okay to call her Olga

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.050
and she was like, "Yeah, whatever".

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:04.575
- What?
(audience and Sarah laugh)

00:08:04.575 --> 00:08:05.670
Like, I'm, I'm freaking,

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.950
I'm so terrified of stuff
like that, not terrified,

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.937
I just don't even wanna know
it exists, if it exists.

00:08:09.937 --> 00:08:12.587
Like, and you're saying it
exists which terrifies me.

00:08:13.746 --> 00:08:15.750
There's just enough
going on in this realm.

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:16.583
- Oh, yeah.

00:08:16.583 --> 00:08:17.416
- [Kelly] I don't wanna have
to worry about another one.

00:08:17.416 --> 00:08:19.500
That's insane and it
didn't scare you at all.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.450
Have you been like that,
like since you were a kid?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.283
- [Sarah] Oh, yes.

00:08:22.283 --> 00:08:24.600
My mom taught me how to read
tarot cards when I was a kid,

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:25.433
she reads palms.

00:08:25.433 --> 00:08:26.730
- I'm obsessed with reading tarot cards,

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:27.660
I think they're so fun.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:29.190
- It's, it's great.
- Yeah.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.650
- It's, it's amazing.
- Sometimes really dead on.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:32.610
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.130
I mean, if you put like
the right energy into it

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:38.100
and ask the right questions,
you can really be able to,

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.750
it's not a future teller by any means,

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.880
but you can really be able
to understand the situation

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.830
where other people are coming from.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.960
But yeah, no, when I
was a, when I was a kid,

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.480
I saw dead people all the time.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.370
- What in the world?
- Yeah.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.900
I can't see them anymore.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.460
- Okay, see that's
what, that's my problem,

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.860
see, I'm a very open person
and that's what scares me,

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:58.260
because I'm, and I, I
literally let people like,

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.330
let go sort of, I'm like,
I walk in somewhere,

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:01.357
and somebody says, I'm like,

00:09:01.357 --> 00:09:02.640
"I'm really cool if you're here.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.574
Like, but like, just don't show yourself".

00:09:04.574 --> 00:09:05.490
(Sarah laughs)

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.530
Like I'm, we can both be
here, we don't have to know.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.135
- I don't wanna know what you look like.

00:09:09.135 --> 00:09:10.800
- Yeah, I'm like, "I don't wanna see you".

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.480
I'm like, because I'm such an open person,

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.730
I feel like they, it would happen to me

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:15.960
and then I would die.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:16.793
- Oh, no.
(Sarah chuckles)

00:09:16.793 --> 00:09:17.626
- Yeah, I would die.

00:09:17.626 --> 00:09:19.080
- You just have to be
able to protect yourself

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:20.150
and it's good.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.517
- I am not that person,
I just like to avoid it.

00:09:22.517 --> 00:09:24.506
So, okay, let's talk about your new show.

00:09:24.506 --> 00:09:27.300
So, it's part of the "Pitch
Perfect" franchise, right?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.133
- Yes.

00:09:28.133 --> 00:09:29.760
- Okay, were you a fan?
Were you just a super fan?

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:30.593
- Such a fan.

00:09:30.593 --> 00:09:31.426
- Me too, I love it.

00:09:31.426 --> 00:09:32.259
- Such a fan.

00:09:32.259 --> 00:09:33.957
- I think I grew up in a choir
like it, so it's like, yeah.

00:09:33.957 --> 00:09:35.310
- Oh, yeah, exactly.
- Yeah.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:38.130
- I mean Jason Moore, who
directed the first one,

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.140
I did "Shrek the Musical"
with him in New York.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.126
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:41.126 --> 00:09:43.170
- And he directed, so
I was such a fan of it.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:46.405
And of course Adam, I know
Adam from "Modern Family"

00:09:46.405 --> 00:09:49.530
so it's such a, an
amazing thing to be able

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.480
to be a part of the whole franchise,

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.250
because I love everyone
that is a part of it.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:54.083
- Yeah.

00:09:54.083 --> 00:09:55.500
- But to be able to sing again,

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.030
I haven't sung in such a long time.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.500
- I was gonna say that's such a cool thing

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.420
that you can do both.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:01.470
What's this plot about?

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:02.730
Like what, what is this story about,

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:04.110
since it's part of the franchise?

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:07.890
- So, Bumper is still
working at the university

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:09.240
and gets a call from,

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:14.240
if anybody remembers Peter
Cromer from the "Pitch Perfect",

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:18.510
I think it was two,
from Das Sound Machine.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:22.740
And he calls him, tells him
that he's famous in Berlin

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:26.010
and that he's going to be
the next biggest thing.

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:29.850
So, Bumper, Adam DeVine
moves to Berlin on a whim

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.530
and I play Peter's assistant

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:34.346
and she's this weird, quirky, bubbly,

00:10:34.346 --> 00:10:37.500
but very, very weird person.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.333
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:38.333 --> 00:10:40.140
- Who is really shy...
- That's fun to play.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:43.320
- And is like a, a very
much a perfectionist.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:45.750
And so, she doesn't want
people to hear her sing

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.310
until she knows it's perfect,

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:48.930
which I can very much relate to.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.310
- I was gonna say, are you that person?

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:51.360
- I am that person.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.270
I am way too much of a control
freak and a perfectionist.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.250
So, I'm very much related to that.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.590
And yeah, it's all about Bumper trying

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.740
to win a thing called,
German Unity Day concert

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.120
for a record label.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.720
- Oh, my God, I'm gonna love it.

